// m21 — "The Verdict" / "Status: Open" (neural-net-history, ch15-s08/s09/s10). CURRENT CLOCK (timeline 2164.00 s):
// window 2065.958–2164.000 (98.042 s), ending at the film's end; fadeIn 0 (it starts on the cut, after m20's beat of
// silence), fadeOut 1 (a safety fade over the last second only: the music is already at the room-tone floor).
// Rubato at 60 BPM: setcps(1), one cycle = one second; every event is written at its ABSOLUTE film second on the
// CURRENT clock through A(t) = t − S, placed by the named word or beat in narration/timeline.json
// (ch15-s08 starts 2065.958, ch15-s09 2109.250, ch15-s10 2135.292; word time = shot start + word start).
// Intensity 0.5, peak 0.7 (the bloom, in the clear).
//
//  ff1-ff5 THE FAST-FORWARD (on the cut, from silence): tape lurch (a string chord spinning up an octave + hiss),
//        then clean: five 0.75-s flashes, each a short forward swell in its era's colour: ff1 valve organ (the knob,
//        A), ff2 bowed glass + cello (snow, Bm), ff3 oscillator (the fans, F#m), ff4 harp (the Go stone, Em), ff5
//        celesta over a soft low D (the wick in the box): the fifth lands on D, alone for 0.8 s before 'Who'.
//  L1527 THE VERDICT: a hush; one dry grey pluck each for RULES ('rules') and KNOWLEDGE ('knowledge'), the same
//        note, no harmony. 'Learning': M1's rising fourth (celesta A in the breath, D struck on the word) as the
//        LEARNING lantern lights, D major in the high strings (a halo). One high harp pluck per accomplice, rising
//        D F# A D (M3's forward pass): data, fire, a messenger, people.
//  L1514 THE NETWORK 'Never one person. The board was a network all along.': M3's forward wave crosses the
//        lantern network, one era instrument per column every 0.44 s (celesta on 'Never', valve organ, cello,
//        piano, oscillator pulse, harp, pizz on 'network'), each rippling D F# A D and staying on as a layer, all
//        at about a third under the line; nothing blooms until it has ended.
//  THE BLOOM in the gap after 'along' (before 'Some'): the trained forward pass D3 F#3 A3 D4 lands on the third,
//        F#: full D major (strings, horns, harp roll, contrabass, one timpani stroke, celesta F#), held, thin
//        before 'Some': the film's fullest moment and the loudest of the score.
//  L1515 THE BAR CHART IN WAX, one celesta note per candle: 'forty' (its length is the contrabass's D), 'two'
//        (short), 'day' (the shortest tick), 'still burn' (a held D: still lit).
//  'dark': everything drops to ONE held note, E (the lit box's question: piano E6, held in strings and glass)
//        through 'how, exactly, it reaches its answers' and L1516b; re-bowed in the clear just after 'open'
//        (strings +0.35 s, piano +0.52 s after the fx-stamp-howfar strike on 'open') and carried to the cut.
//  THE LAST SLIP (ch15-s09 cut): solo celesta, the slip motif with m12's pitches (written a3 -> d4), slowed:
//        the A an upbeat out of the held E, the D struck on the cut, decayed before L1517 starts. L1517 itself is left bare; the strings take the D only AFTER 'seventeen', in
//        the breath before the quote, and a soft A-E fifth slides in beneath after 'future'; the quote (L1518)
//        over the held D; gone before the stamp.
//  SILENCE: the stamp (s09 b3, 0.5 s after 'said') and the lamp click (b4) sound on the foley bus alone.
//  L1520 M4's walk, solo cello, very soft, below D3: A1 D2 E2 F2 G2 ('rim') F2 E2 C2 D2, home before 'That'.
//  'new' the match (foley) in near silence; 'candles' the wick catches: one tiny damped celesta glint.
//  THE LAST GESTURE, in the clear after 'from' as the flame stands: celesta M1 rises once more, A->D, held (the
//        high strings take the D); into the cut to black (ch15-s10) the strings and contrabass slide in beneath
//        it to A-E: Asus4, the held D the suspension; a solo cello takes the held D at D3. It does NOT resolve.
//  ch15-s10 THE END CARDS (v8, the 28.71-s card sequence: Turing b1-b2, CREDITS b2-sources, SOURCES sources-b3):
//        the suspension kept alive as a ppp string pad (lpf 1200): A-E + D through the Turing card; the fifth lets
//        go into b2 and the D ALONE is HELD under the CREDITS card, bowed twice (the second bowing crossfades in
//        halfway through the card with a faint upper octave, the flame breathing once) at about -34 LUFS M, never
//        a decay to silence; on `sources` one soft celesta D and the pad lets go with it, both ringing down to the
//        floor before the fade to black (b3) and the safety fade.
//
//  v3-v7: see score/notes-history.json. v8 (2026-10-13, round-4 re-fit): ch15-s08/s09 and the Turing card moved
//        bodily +3.75 s (no line inside them changed length); the CREDITS card is 12.8 s (was 6.1): the lone D is
//        bowed twice and held to `sources`; the SOURCES celesta moved with its card.
setcps(1)
const S = 2065.9583
const A = (t) => +(t - S).toFixed(3)
const N = 99        // seconds covered by each compiled sequence (the window is 98.042 s, to the film's end)
const G = 2.0       // master trim (postgain): old-clock render 5 measured -22.0 LUFS at 2.0 (bloom -14.7 M);
                    // new-clock v1 -22.4, but the beds under L1527/L1515/L1517 sat only 1-7 dB under the voice:
                    // v2 lowers every layer under a line (the hush, Learning, the slip, the walk) and keeps the gaps
const W3 = 1 / 3    // the network's era layers under L1514: about a third of their velocity (review, MAJOR)
const WH = .5       // v5: the HIGH era layers (celesta, piano, harp, top strings) a further -6 dB: L1514's 1-4 kHz
                    // band (the consonants of the thesis line) measured only 1.7 dB clear of them in v4

// ---- shared helper: events in cue-local SECONDS (setcps(1): one cycle = one second = one beat at 60 BPM) ----
// [start, dur, notes, velocity, {per-event params}] compiled into one mini-notation sequence per lane
// (overlapping events go to new lanes), so every onset sits exactly where the clock needs it.
function line(evs, defs) {
  defs = defs || {}
  const sorted = [...evs].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0])
  const lanes = []
  for (const e of sorted) {
    if (e[0] < -1e-6 || e[0] >= N) throw new Error("m21: event outside the window at cue second " + e[0])
    let lane = lanes.find((l) => l.end <= e[0] + 1e-6)
    if (!lane) { lane = { end: 0, evs: [] }; lanes.push(lane) }
    lane.evs.push(e)
    lane.end = e[0] + e[1]
  }
  const keys = Object.keys(defs)
  const seq = (lane, val) => {
    let pos = 0
    const out = []
    for (const e of lane.evs) {
      if (e[0] - pos > 1e-6) out.push('~@' + (e[0] - pos).toFixed(4))
      out.push(val(e) + '@' + e[1].toFixed(4))
      pos = e[0] + e[1]
    }
    if (N - pos > 1e-6) out.push('~@' + (N - pos).toFixed(4))
    return mini('[' + out.join(' ') + ']')
  }
  return stack(...lanes.map((lane) => {
    let p = note(seq(lane, (e) => e[2])).velocity(seq(lane, (e) => e[3]))
    for (const k of keys) p = p[k](seq(lane, (e) => (e[4] && e[4][k] != null ? e[4][k] : defs[k])))
    return p.slow(N).postgain(G)
  }))
}

// ---- THE FAST-FORWARD ----
// tape lurch: a low string chord that spins up an octave as the tape catches, with a breath of hiss
$: line([[A(2066.061), .8, '[d2,a2,d3]', .2]], { attack: .3, release: .25 })
  .s('gm_string_ensemble_1').penv(12).pattack(.7).lpf(1600).room(.3).rsize(2).orbit(1)
$: line([[A(2066.061), .85, 'd4', .5]], { attack: .45, release: .2 })
  .s('pink').hpf(1200).lpf(6000).gain(.05).orbit(1)
// the forward swells (strings): A, Bm, F#m, Em, then a soft D that stays for the hush
$: line([
  [A(2066.961), .5, '[a2,e3,a3,c#4]', .15], [A(2067.711), .5, '[b2,f#3,b3,d4]', .15], [A(2068.461), .5, '[f#2,c#3,f#3,a3]', .15],
  [A(2069.211), .5, '[e2,b2,e3,g3]', .15],
  [A(2069.961), 5.6, '[d2,a2,d3]', .045, { attack: .5, release: 1.6, lpf: 800 }],
], { attack: .3, release: .35, lpf: 2200 })
  .s('gm_string_ensemble_1').room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)
// each era's colour on its flash
$: line([[A(2066.961), .5, '[a3,e4]', .24]], { attack: .2, release: .3 }).s('gm_drawbar_organ').lpf(1500).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2067.711), .5, '[f#4,b4]', .16]], { attack: .25, release: .4 }).s('gm_pad_bowed').room(.5).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2067.711), .5, 'b2', .22]], { attack: .2, release: .4 }).s('gm_cello').lpf(1200).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2068.461), .5, '[f#2,c#3,f#3]', .5]], { attack: .2, release: .3 }).s('sawtooth').lpf(1300).gain(.12).room(.3).rsize(3).orbit(2)
$: line([[A(2069.211), .5, '[e3,b3,e4,g4]', .2]], { release: 1 }).s('gm_orchestral_harp').room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(2)

// ---- THE VERDICT: grey plucks (dry, same note), then LEARNING and its accomplices ----
$: line([[A(2072.301), .2, 'e2', .28], [A(2073.691), .2, 'e2', .28]], { release: .15 })
  .s('gm_pizzicato_strings').lpf(650).room(.08).rsize(1).orbit(3)
// one high harp pluck per accomplice (above the voice): D F# A D, M3's forward pass, the last left ringing
$: line([
  // v6: D5-D6 sit in the vowel band under the line: -4.4 dB and damped (L1527's 250-2k band was 9.7 dB clear, ~0 on 'messenger')
  [A(2077.721), .5, 'd5', .045], [A(2078.441), .5, 'f#5', .045], [A(2079.311), .5, 'a5', .045], [A(2080.471), .5, 'd6', .03, { release: .5 }],   // v8: 'people' (D6 1-4k 1.2 dB): halved, short ring
